.TH QUADRF-NTSC 1 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-ntsc \- decode and play an analogue video signal
.br
quadrf-ntsc-demod \- NTSC demodulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-ntsc
.br
.B quadrf-ntsc-demod
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadrf-ntsc
is the Camera Decoder launcher. It tunes the front-end with
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
runs the demodulator and pipes the result into mpv. The video output is chosen
from the environment: inside a graphical session mpv draws there, and only on a
bare console with a monitor attached does it go straight to KMS.
.PP
.B quadrf-ntsc-demod
reads IQ from the SoapySDR device, demodulates NTSC and writes raw yuyv422
frames at 640x480 on standard output. It is usually driven by
.BR quadrf-ntsc ,
but the raw stream can equally be redirected to a file or piped into ffmpeg.
.B --dump_ppm
.I dir
writes decoded frames as PPM stills;
.B --dump_count
.I n
stops after
.I n
dumped frames (skip
.B --dump_after
frames first so lock can settle);
.B --duration
.I s
exits after
.I s
seconds.
.PP
The launcher starts on Raceband 5 (5806 MHz) and shows a short on-screen
reminder of the keys. The mpv window must have keyboard focus (click it).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Step channel 1–8 in the current band and retune the RX LO. The channel
name and frequency flash on screen for about 1.5 s. Mouse wheel does the
same.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Change FPV band (Race, A, B, E, F). Channel number is kept (e.g. R5 to
A5). Default band is Race.
.TP
.BR s ", " S
Decrease or increase color saturation in steps of 10%.
.TP
.BR c
Toggle between color and monochrome (grayscale) display.
.TP
.BR r
Reset saturation to 100% color.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Toggle the on-screen command list / keyboard shortcuts reference.
.TP
.BR q ", " Escape
Quit mpv (stops the decoder).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/quadrf/ntsc_ch.lua
mpv script that maps Up/Down onto channel and Left/Right onto band, then
calls
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
.IR freq= .
.SH BUGS
The decoder currently misbehaves when an HDMI display is attached to the Pi.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR mpv (1)
